+### Action work: reuse the existing checker first
+
+Keep three costs separate: per-target action construction/owner assignment (bypassed by an accepted configured-target hit), cross-target output conflict checking (still required), and execution sharing (still required). The delivered change claims each starting root in the existing conflict finder's visited set and avoids only a provably repeated same-object comparison during owner assignment. Conflict reruns keep fresh visited sets and predecessor completion ordering. The existing set can gain one entry per unique starting root; do not describe this as a guaranteed memory reduction.
+
+Measure disjoint and overlapping top-level closures with the action-heavy fixture. Require identical default-output hashes and cold, restored/local, restored/restored conflict cases. Avoid a global action-key memo: output owner identity changes during assignment, and action retention already has lifecycle owners. A future conflict-summary experiment must authenticate exact closure/action revisions and output namespace/configuration, then still check new composition boundaries for same-path and prefix conflicts. Do not skip those intersections based on a valid Skycache payload. This is an independent checker refinement, not completion of P03 publication reuse or P09 provenance migration.
+
